  "id": "papompang_toraja",
  "name": "Pa'pompang (Toraja bamboo band)",
  "family": "global",
  "lineage": "Bamboo band of Tana Toraja in South Sulawesi that took shape in the mid-twentieth century as a local adaptation of European wind instruments, introduced through schools and the church, with gospel teachers playing a large part; it has since gained sacred standing as a marker of Torajan identity. Large sets of pompang, blown bamboo tubes of graded sizes made from petung and tallang bamboo (the generic horn card stands in), sound chords under the melody of a few suling bamboo flutes (the generic bamboo-flute card stands in), with a drum (the generic membrane-drum card stands in). Bands play at rambu solo' funerals, rambu tuka' thanksgiving rites and church services.",
